 2. 🚨 CNN: Chatbot blunder &quot;almost started a war&quot; 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Brendan Lynch/Axios

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 The intelligence report rocketed around the U.S. military last spring: A Chinese ship in the Middle East was transporting nuclear-weapon components, CNN's Katie Bo Lillis and Zachary Cohen report. 

 Preparations to intercept started immediately. Armed U.S. military members were ready to board the ship. Planes were in the air. 🤖 But the report that "almost started a war" was "entirely false," a source told CNN. 

 A special operations analyst had used a chatbot to help generate the report, and the AI had misidentified what was on the ship. Keep reading . 

 
 
