 7. 🎨 Presidential portraits 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Photo: George W. Bush Presidential Center. Cover: Crown

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Former President George W. Bush has a new book of oil paintings coming on March 9, featuring his oil portraits of political prisoners and dissidents.

 " The Call of Freedom : Portraits of Political Prisoners and Dissidents" will include Bush's portraits of such symbols of oppression as the late Mahsa Amini , whose death in 2022 while in the custody of Iranian authorities led to nationwide protests, and the imprisoned Nicaraguan bishop Rolando José Álvarez Lagos . Former Soviet Union dissident Natan Sharansky is contributing a foreword. ( AP ) Bush, 80, writes: "This book, coupled with our work at the Bush Institute, is a chance for me to send a message that the United States cares deeply about people seeking freedom. And hopefully these stories will remind us that we who live in liberty have a duty to stand with those who do not."

