 8. 🍲 Lingo for the road: &quot;Food divorce&quot; 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Shoshana Gordon/Axios

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 For some couples, the secret to staying together is eating apart.

 Coordinating daily meals can be exhausting. "Mismatched work shifts, meal-prep burnout, strict diets, and the explosion of GLP-1 medications like Ozempic have only amplified the divide," the New York Post reports. So people are trialing "food divorce": You figure out your meals, and I'll figure out mine.

